import OIBridge.RouteB

/-!
# The manuscript-axiom audit — A1–A6 against the substratum witness

Route B1 (`RouteB.routeB_target`) exhibits `substratumTheory (Fin 2)`, the theory generated by the
monomial class, as a two-state theory satisfying `DerivedOICore` and failing phase-free richness.
`DerivedOI` is the kernel's closure; the manuscripts' own structural assumptions are A1–A6 of
`[Substratum §3.1]`: finiteness of the configuration space, bijectivity of the dynamics, bounded
coupling degree, center independence, linearity of the wave equation, background independence.
This file is the preregistered pass of `MANUSCRIPT-AXIOM-AUDIT.md`: each axiom is tested against
the witness under a faithful theory-level form where one exists, and recorded as a formalization
gap where none does.

## What is representable

Every one of A1–A6 is a condition on a substratum `(S, φ)`. What a `FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2)`
carries of a substratum is the sealed OI core, `Core` with the dynamics `sigmaPerm`, embedded at
level four by `coreIdx` and realized by the theory. So A1 and A2 have faithful theory-level forms
relative to that realized core (`A1Realized`, `A2Realized`), and both hold for the witness
(`substratumTheory_A1`, `substratumTheory_A2`); A1 holds for every theory by the interface's
types (`a1_every_theory`), and A2 holds for every theory with composite unitary control as well
(`a2_of_control`). A3–A6 need a site type, a coupling graph with a uniform degree bound, lattice
translations, an additive alphabet with an additive update rule, and internal indices with a
coupling matrix; the interface has none of these, and no weakened predicate is defined for them.
The conjunction of the two representable axioms is `A1A2Realized`; it is not the manuscript OI
and is not named so.

## The configuration-level sourcing bound

The gap has one cause. A3–A6 constrain the form of `(S, φ)`, and the kernel's sourcing of
operations from a substratum is configuration-level: the substratum's direct interventions are
bijections of its configurations and phases, whose operators are monomial. For any
implementation architecture all of whose admissible operators are monomial
(`ConfigurationLevel`), the generated theory's availability is contained in the substratum
theory's (`configurationLevel_availExt_le`), the falsifier `rot` is unavailable on the two-state
carrier (`configurationLevel_falsifierUnavailable`), and, when the class is label-invariant
(configuration relabelling is gauge), the generated theory fails phase-free richness and is not
exact finite operational quantum mechanics (`configurationLevel_not_phaseFree`,
`configurationLevel_not_qm`). The substratum class is the largest configuration-level
architecture (`substratumClass_configurationLevel`, `configurationLevel_iff_le_substratum`).

The reading, fixed in the audit note before the proof: whatever conditions are placed on
`(S, φ)`, a configuration-level sourcing lands inside the monomial theory, which is the B1 witness;
phase-free richness can enter only through a sourcing that is not configuration-level, the
observer-level lift, whose derivation the manuscripts record as open. Nothing here says whether
that lift is derivable.
-/

namespace OIBridge
namespace ManuscriptAxioms

open Complex Matrix CoherentLift CoherentExtension SpectatorBridge OperationalAssembly
open AncillaClosure MonoidalCompletion InterventionLocality MicroReversibility PrimitiveSource
open LieRankSource DiagonalTheory SubstratumInterface StructuralClosure MinimalRepertoire
open LevelOneSeam PhysicalCharacterization OIRealization IndependenceCensus RouteB

/-! ### Section A — A1 and A2, the representable axioms, relative to the realized core -/

section Representable

/-- **A1, REALIZED**: the configuration space of the realized substratum is finite. The core has
eight states, and every level of the theory is a finite type of `2 n` states. The predicate does
not depend on the theory: A1 is carried by the interface's types. -/
def A1Realized (_T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2)) : Prop :=
  Fintype.card Core = 8 ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, Fintype.card (Fin 2 × Fin n) = 2 * n

/-- **A2, REALIZED**: the realized dynamics `sigmaPerm` is a bijection of the core, realized as a
one-outcome (deterministic) transported permutation channel at level four, and its inverse is
realized likewise (reversible). -/
def A2Realized (T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2)) : Prop :=
  T.availExt 4 Unit (fun _ => transport coreIdx (correlationExtension sigmaPerm (onesCorr Core)))
    ∧ T.availExt 4 Unit
        (fun _ => transport coreIdx (correlationExtension sigmaPerm.symm (onesCorr Core)))

/-- The conjunction of the two representable axioms. Not the manuscript OI: A3–A6 have no
faithful form in this interface. -/
def A1A2Realized (T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2)) : Prop :=
  A1Realized T ∧ A2Realized T

/-- **A1 HOLDS FOR EVERY THEORY**, by the interface's types. -/
theorem a1_every_theory (T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2)) : A1Realized T :=
  ⟨sealedCore_is_finiteOI.1, fun n => by simp⟩

/-- **A1 HOLDS FOR THE WITNESS.** -/
theorem substratumTheory_A1 : A1Realized (substratumTheory (Fin 2)) :=
  a1_every_theory _

/-- **A2 HOLDS FOR THE WITNESS**: both transported permutation channels come from monomial
generation alone (`substratumTheory_relabel`). -/
theorem substratumTheory_A2 : A2Realized (substratumTheory (Fin 2)) :=
  ⟨substratumTheory_relabel sigmaPerm, substratumTheory_relabel sigmaPerm.symm⟩

/-- **A1 AND A2 HOLD FOR THE WITNESS.** -/
theorem substratumTheory_A1A2 : A1A2Realized (substratumTheory (Fin 2)) :=
  ⟨substratumTheory_A1, substratumTheory_A2⟩

/-- **A2 HOLDS FOR EVERY THEORY WITH COMPOSITE UNITARY CONTROL**, so for quantum mechanics: the
axiom does not separate the witness from quantum mechanics. -/
theorem a2_of_control (T : FiniteOperationalTheory (Fin 2)) (hctrl : HasCompositeUnitaryControl T) :
    A2Realized T :=
  ⟨relabel_available T hctrl sigmaPerm, relabel_available T hctrl sigmaPerm.symm⟩

end Representable

/-! ### Section B — the configuration-level sourcing bound -/

section Sourcing

/-- **A CONFIGURATION-LEVEL ARCHITECTURE**: every admissible implementation operator is monomial,
a permutation of the configurations composed with a phase — the operator shape of every direct
intervention on a substratum's configurations. -/
def ConfigurationLevel (𝓘 : ImplementationClass) : Prop :=
  ∀ (S : Type) [Fintype S] [DecidableEq S] (K : Matrix S S ℂ), 𝓘 S K → IsMonomial K

/-- The substratum class is configuration-level. -/
theorem substratumClass_configurationLevel : ConfigurationLevel substratumClass :=
  fun _ _ _ _ h => h

/-- **THE SUBSTRATUM CLASS IS THE LARGEST CONFIGURATION-LEVEL ARCHITECTURE**: a class is
configuration-level exactly when it is contained in the substratum class. -/
theorem configurationLevel_iff_le_substratum (𝓘 : ImplementationClass) :
    ConfigurationLevel 𝓘
      ↔ ∀ (S : Type) [Fintype S] [DecidableEq S] (K : Matrix S S ℂ), 𝓘 S K → substratumClass S K :=
  Iff.rfl

variable {𝓘 : ImplementationClass} (arch : Architecture 𝓘)
variable {A : Type} [Fintype A] [DecidableEq A]

/-- **A CONFIGURATION-LEVEL SOURCING LANDS INSIDE THE SUBSTRATUM THEORY**: every instrument
family available in the theory a configuration-level architecture generates is available in the
theory the monomial class generates, on every carrier and at every level. -/
theorem configurationLevel_availExt_le (h : ConfigurationLevel 𝓘) {n : ℕ} {O : Type} [Fintype O]
    [DecidableEq O] (F : O → Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ →ₗ[ℂ] Matrix (A × Fin n) (A × Fin n) ℂ)
    (hF : (genTheory 𝓘 arch A).availExt n O F) : (substratumTheory A).availExt n O F := by
  obtain ⟨hreal, htr⟩ := hF
  refine ⟨fun a => ?_, htr⟩
  obtain ⟨ι, _, K, hK, hadm⟩ := hreal a
  exact ⟨ι, inferInstance, K, hK, fun i => h _ _ (hadm i)⟩

/-- **THE FALSIFIER IS UNAVAILABLE IN EVERY CONFIGURATION-LEVEL SOURCING**: an available
conjugation is a sum of monomial conjugations, each preserving the diagonal, which `rot` does
not. -/
theorem configurationLevel_falsifierUnavailable (h : ConfigurationLevel 𝓘) :
    FalsifierUnavailable (genTheory 𝓘 arch (Fin 2)) := by
  intro hav
  obtain ⟨ι, _, K, hK, hadm⟩ := hav.1 ()
  have hK' : conjChannel rot = ∑ i, conjChannel (K i) := hK
  apply rot_not_preservesDiag
  rw [hK']
  exact preservesDiag_sum _ _ fun i _ => preservesDiag_conj_of_monomial (h _ _ (hadm i))

/-- **NO CONFIGURATION-LEVEL SOURCING HAS PHASE-FREE RICHNESS** on the two-state carrier, when
configuration relabelling is gauge (the class is label-invariant, so the generated theory has
embedded observation and the falsifier reduction applies). -/
theorem configurationLevel_not_phaseFree (h : ConfigurationLevel 𝓘) (hl : LabelInvariant 𝓘) :
    ¬ PhaseFreeRichness (genTheory 𝓘 arch (Fin 2)) :=
  not_phaseFree_of_falsifier_unavailable _ (genTheory_embeddedObservation 𝓘 arch hl)
    (configurationLevel_falsifierUnavailable arch h)

/-- **NO CONFIGURATION-LEVEL SOURCING IS QUANTUM MECHANICS** on the two-state carrier. -/
theorem configurationLevel_not_qm (h : ConfigurationLevel 𝓘) :
    ¬ ExactAllFiniteEndomorphicQuantumOps (genTheory 𝓘 arch (Fin 2)) :=
  fun hqm => qm_not_falsifierUnavailable _ hqm (configurationLevel_falsifierUnavailable arch h)

end Sourcing

